# Research never ships — plan/ is always ignored
# Anchored: an unanchored `plan/` also matched init/src/plan/, so a new file there was
# silently untracked. Same bug as `build/` vs adapters/build/, fixed the same way.
/plan/

# Cloud control plane — the paid app (moat + tenant/billing) lives OUTSIDE this repo, at the
# sibling ReticleHQ/app/, with its own git per service. This entry is a belt-and-suspenders guard
# so a stray app/ dir can never be committed into the Apache OSS repo by accident.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose. A bare `app/` matches a directory called `app` at ANY depth, which
# silently swallowed the Next.js App Router routes in apps/next-smoke/app/ — the server-actions,
# RSC and idle-stream routes the e2e battery drives. They existed locally, so every gate passed,
# while a fresh clone got a next-smoke app missing the routes its own spec tests. Only files
# already tracked before the rule landed (layout.tsx, page.tsx) survived, which is what made it
# invisible.
/app/

# Marketing: keep the source (HTML/CSS/mjs) reproducible, but never commit the heavy
# render outputs or raw footage — host those on a CDN / GitHub Releases. The curated
# README media lives in assets/readme/ (a separate dir) and IS committed.
assets/clips/
assets/*.png
assets/marketing/**/*.mp4
assets/marketing/**/*.mov
assets/marketing/**/*.gif
assets/marketing/**/*.png

# Image-generation SOURCE split: the benchmark card generators (assets/benchmarks/render.mjs +
# src/bench-*.html) and the shared design system (assets/marketing/src/_system.css) are PUBLIC —
# they generate the committed README/docs images. The GTM/marketing source stays LOCAL (design
# reference, never shipped to the public repo).
assets/marketing/render.mjs
assets/marketing/demo/
assets/marketing/reels/
assets/marketing/video/
assets/marketing/landscape/
assets/marketing/v0.5.0/
assets/marketing/src/*.html

# Env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies
# No trailing slash, deliberately. `node_modules/` matches DIRECTORIES only, and a package manager
# that links a workspace's modules leaves a SYMLINK of that name, which is a file. Those were not
# ignored, so `git add -A` committed them, and the branch then carried a file where CI needed a
# directory: every job died at install with ENOTDIR before reaching the change.
node_modules
.pnpm-store/

# Build output
dist/
/build/
.next/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Rust build output for the Tauri smoke app (multi-GB; never committed)
apps/tauri-smoke/src-tauri/target/
adapters/realm/tauri/target/
apps/tauri-smoke/src-tauri/Cargo.lock
apps/tauri-smoke/src-tauri/gen/

# Test / coverage
coverage/

# Python (not used here, kept for parity with the foundation skill)
__pycache__/
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Graphify artifacts
graph.json
graph.html
graphify-out/
GRAPH_REPORT.md

# Reticle: commit the shareable project config (cloud binding, flows, baselines); ignore local runtime
# artifacts at ANY depth (root app + apps/*/). The SECRET api key is never here — it lives in
# ~/.reticle/credentials.json (outside the repo). `**/` so nested demo apps are covered too.
**/.reticle/runs/
**/.reticle/project.json
**/.reticle/*.log

# Logs / OS
*.log
.DS_Store

# local registry auth token (never commit)
.npmrc

# Issuer signing keys — the license-minting private key NEVER touches git.
# (Public keys are baked into a release via env, not committed here either.)
*.pem
*.key
issuer-*.json

# Playwright MCP session dumps (written to cwd during benchmark runs)
.playwright-mcp/

# Agent git worktrees (never track — they are live checkouts)
.claude/worktrees/
.cursor/worktrees/
leads/

# Playwright CLI benchmark disk artifacts (snapshots/console logs)
.playwright-cli/
/docs-api/

# The TRANSIENT half of a Reticle workspace, at any depth. NOT a blanket ignore: a bare `.reticle/`
# matches everywhere and would swallow the shareable half inside `apps/` too, which is a different
# decision from the one made below for this repository's own root.
#
# Keep this list in step with TRANSIENT in server/src/features/journal/on-disk/workspace-gitignore.ts
# — that is the file users get, and this is the same decision made for ourselves.
**/.reticle/sessions/
**/.reticle/visual/
**/.reticle/feedback/
**/.reticle/ambient.json
**/.reticle/envelopes.json
**/.reticle/flake.json
**/.reticle/assertion-tiers.json
**/.reticle/impact.json
**/.reticle/cloud-state.json
**/.reticle/issues.json
**/.reticle/*.tmp

# THIS repository's own workspace, shareable half included — contract.json, flows/, capsules/,
# intent.json. Root-anchored, so it says nothing about the fixtures under `apps/`.
#
# These used to be tracked deliberately, to make this repo eat its own dog food: a saved flow only
# earns its keep when a teammate or CI can replay it, and that is what Reticle writes into every
# user's `.reticle/.gitignore`. That is no longer the decision here — the gates rewrite these on
# every run, so what was committed was whichever drive happened to go last rather than a flow
# anybody chose to keep, and the diff was noise on unrelated pull requests.
#
# One line to reverse: delete this block and `git add -f .reticle/`.
/.reticle/
# Everything under apps/ is a local fixture, and its whole workspace is generated by whichever gate
# last drove it — the e2e battery re-records `flows/attach-a-file.json` on every run. Shareable-half
# rules do not apply to a directory nobody is meant to read.
apps/**/.reticle/

# Complex app fixtures now live in their own repo, reticle-fixtures — see docs/fixtures.md.
# They are somebody else's apps at real scale, with their own package managers (react-admin is a
# yarn monorepo, which breaks this pnpm workspace the moment it sits under apps/*), and they need
# a branch model this repo cannot give them: a pristine `clean` branch to install into, because a
# fresh install is only meaningful on a surface that has never seen Reticle.

# Copied into server/ at prepack so the skill and docs ship with the CLI users npx.
# The originals at the repo root are the only editable copies.
/server/SKILL.md
/server/docs/

# Maintainer rules for GitHub conduct — issues, PRs, releases. Deliberately private: it names the
# mistakes that produced each rule, and those belong to the people who made them, not to the repo.
/GITHUB.md
conformance/.handoff/

# Local Verdaccio state (scripts/local-registry.sh). Beside its config so it resolves the same
# on every OS; see the note in scripts/verdaccio.yaml.
scripts/.local-registry/

# Local product-smoke evidence; uploaded by CI.
/artifacts/smoke/
/artifacts/install-packages/
/artifacts/install-sandbox/
